<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vincent Auriol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1966">1966</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vincent Auriol was a French Socialist politician and the first President of the French Fourth Republic, from 1947 to 1954. A former finance minister under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leon-blum">Léon Blum</a>, he presided over the Constituent Assembly in 1946 and as president oversaw frequent changes of government in the post-war republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vincent-auriol.jpg" alt="Vincent Auriol" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author (Studio Harcourt) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_officiel_Vincent_Auriol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
